Zensus 2022, population per 100 m grid cell
-------------------------------------------

Dataset: population_cells (8,351 populated 100 m squares whose middle lies
in Leipzig, 599,035 people)

Publisher: the Statistical Offices of the Federation and the Länder
(Statistische Ämter des Bundes und der Länder), the 2022 census's
population per grid cell, published by the Statistisches Bundesamt in
2024.
https://www.zensus2022.de/DE/Ergebnisse-des-Zensus/gitterzellen.html

Licence: Data licence Germany, attribution, version 2.0 (DL-DE-BY-2.0),
as the archive's own description of the data states it: "Die mit dieser
Datensatzbeschreibung beschriebenen Daten aus dem Datenangebot der
Statistischen Ämter des Bundes und der Länder sind lizenziert unter der
Datenlizenz Deutschland – Namensnennung – Version 2.0 (dl-de/by-2-0;
http://www.govdata.de/dl-de/by-2-0)."
https://www.govdata.de/dl-de/by-2-0

Credit: © Statistische Ämter des Bundes und der Länder, 2024 (Zensus
2022), the notice the description carries.

Where and when: read on 2026-10-25:

  https://www.destatis.de/static/DE/zensus/gitterdaten/Zensus2022_Bevoelkerungszahl.zip
  (18,501,524 bytes, SHA-256 1a8428d31eab264c8717bfdcbf40fbd66c217edb2e2a98d0e67741bd8a1a941a;
  the grid file Zensus2022_Bevoelkerungszahl_100m-Gitter.csv and the
  description Datensatzbeschreibung_Bevoelkerungszahl_Gitterzellen.xlsx
  inside it)

Kept: the cells whose middle lies in one of Leipzig's 63 districts, each
with its grid id and its people, drawn as its 100 m square turned from the
European grid (ETRS89-LAEA, EPSG:3035) into longitude and latitude. Left
out: every other cell of Germany. This is a modified version of the data.
The census applies a secrecy procedure to keep people from being
identified, so a single cell's number may differ a little from the count.


OpenStreetMap
-------------

Dataset: supermarkets (272 supermarkets, 216 of them in the city)

Publisher: the OpenStreetMap contributors, read through the Overpass API.
https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright

Licence: Open Database License 1.0 (ODbL-1.0). The ODbL applies to this
dataset as a derived database: anyone may use it, and a public derived
database must be offered under the ODbL as well.
https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/

Credit: © OpenStreetMap contributors.

Where and when: read on 2026-10-25 from the Overpass API, the data as of
2026-10-25 13:04:21 UTC, with this query:

  https://overpass-api.de/api/interpreter
  [out:json][timeout:120];nwr["shop"="supermarket"](51.2,12.17,51.48,12.6);out center tags;

Kept: each shop's OpenStreetMap id, name and brand (its name where no
brand is tagged), placed at the node or, for a shop mapped as a building,
at the building's centre. A shop mapped twice, as a point and as its
building, within 50 m and under one brand, is kept once. Left out: every
other tag. This is a modified version of the data.


